        "entry_wwqCPr": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "How does a vacuum cleaner work?",
            "text": "<p>A vacuum cleaner utilises an electric motor to drive a series of fans which in turn generate an airflow to create suction force. This is used to pull up and draw in dirt and dust from floor surfaces via an intake port. Debris is pulled and trapped into a collection bin or bag before the exhaust air is expelled back into the room via a filter which is designed to trap fine particles and allergens. </p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
